From 82e52092b10d9271a76b78f68839f37511d7062e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:24:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vout: select the subtitles of a picture forced on screen at
 the time it is shown

The output selects the subtitles drawn over a picture at the picture's
date, and deletes those over by then. A picture forced on screen is
shown at once, not at its date, and the first one of a start or a seek is
forced while the input still buffers: its date was converted by the clock
before the end of the buffering moved its origin, and stood up to the
length buffered (0.6 s) later than the pictures after it. When the
subtitle due at the position, which the decoder sends once the buffering
ends, reached the output before that picture was shown, it was judged
over at that date and deleted, and none of the pictures after it drew
it: a seek inside a cue showed no subtitle until the next cue, at times.

Select the subtitles of a picture forced on screen while playing at the
time it is shown. A paused output still selects them at its pause date.
---
 src/video_output/video_output.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_output/video_output.c b/src/video_output/video_output.c
index f20800b..9932e79 100644
--- a/src/video_output/video_output.c
+++ b/src/video_output/video_output.c
@@ -990,6 +990,15 @@ static int ThreadDisplayRenderPicture(vout_thread_t *vout, bool is_forced)
     vlc_tick_t render_subtitle_date;
     if (vout->p->pause.is_on)
         render_subtitle_date = vout->p->pause.date;
+    else if (vout->p->displayed.current->b_force)
+        /* A picture forced on screen is shown at once, not at its date, and
+         * the first one of a start or a seek is forced while the input still
+         * buffers: its date was converted by the clock before the end of the
+         * buffering moved its origin, up to the length buffered later than
+         * the pictures after it. Selected at that date, a subtitle due at the
+         * position the decoder sent meanwhile was judged over and deleted,
+         * and none of the pictures after it drew it. It is seen now. */
+        render_subtitle_date = mdate();
     else
         render_subtitle_date = filtered->date > 1 ? filtered->date : mdate();
     vlc_tick_t render_osd_date = mdate(); /* FIXME wrong */
